//----------------------------------------------------
// BEST PRACTICES & TIPS FOR DESIGNING STATE MACHINES
//----------------------------------------------------
// 1) Ensure All States Are Unique and Non-Overlapping
//    - Each state should be mutually exclusive unless hierarchical states are needed.
//    - Overlapping states might introduce conflicting logic.
//
// 2) Define Clear State Transitions
//    - Avoid jumping between unrelated states without a logical progression.
//    - Ensure transitions are documented and follow a clear flow.
//
// 3) Use Meaningful State Names
//    - Instead of magic numbers (1,2,3), use descriptive constants (e.g., STATE_IDLE, STATE_BUY_SETUP).
//    - Improves readability and debugging.
//
// 4) Prevent Unreachable or "Zombie" States
//    - Ensure every state has a way to transition forward or reset to neutral.
//    - Avoid states that can be entered but never exited unless intentional.
//
// 5) Use a Neutral or Default State
//    - A fallback/reset state helps recover from unexpected conditions.
//
// 6) Handle Errors Gracefully
//    - Detect invalid transitions and log issues for debugging.
//    - Use assertion functions or transition logs to validate correctness.
//
// 7) Ensure Logical Transition Timing
//    - Avoid reacting to noisy or single-bar conditions.
//    - Consider requiring multiple confirmations before changing state.
//
// 8) Use `printOverlappingTransitions()` for Debugging
//    - Helps detect unintended state changes occurring on the same bar.
//    - Useful for identifying high-speed execution conflicts.
//
// 9) Document Your State Machine
//    - Maintain a transition table describing state behavior and possible transitions.
//    - Helps ensure long-term maintainability.
//
// 10) Test Your State Machine Extensively
//    - Run unit tests and assertions to verify expected transitions.
//    - Perform backtesting and live logging to validate state behavior.
//
// Example Transition Table:
// | State                 | Description                | Transitions To          |
// |-----------------------|--------------------------|------------------------|
// | STATE_IDLE           | Waiting for a signal      | STATE_BUY_SETUP        |
// | STATE_BUY_SETUP      | Buy conditions forming    | STATE_BUY_EXECUTED     |
// | STATE_BUY_EXECUTED   | Buy executed             | STATE_SELL_SETUP, IDLE |
// | STATE_SELL_SETUP     | Sell conditions forming  | STATE_SELL_EXECUTED    |
//
// Following these best practices ensures a structured, reliable, and maintainable state machine design.
//----------------------------------------------------
